- path-root-handling (quickjs-path.c): `path` mishandles the root directory.
  resolve('/') returns "<cwd>/\0", resolve('/a/..') returns "", and
  dirname('/') and dirname('/x') return "." instead of "/". lib/module.js
  carries its own posix helpers to avoid it. found while writing the
  node:module port.

    import * as path from 'path';
